<title>USA: WesterFed stake cut by Cramer group.</title>
<headline>WesterFed stake cut by Cramer group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investor James Cramer said it cut its stake in WesterFed Financial Corp to 255,000 common shares or 4.6 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it most recently sold a net 45,000 shares between May 6 and May 15 at $19.13 to $20.06 each.</p>
<p>WesterFed, based in Missoula, Mont., is the holding company for Western Federal Savings Bank.</p>
